#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4df33ff-e04e-55ec-b273-9eceff7db53b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rotation Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa58e3f-1404-5bee-89f4-249fd02760ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/39168e3de9d42254e0c1528ab7ed40f2a4c0e88e9570705b773e3875d5057df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283727} {:answer/id #uuid "f8aad999-521b-5aaf-89a4-73a2f1cffc33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/b66fd6bb3e9b37fd3a72927a1fb4df87eaffea3bf5579e681fee3aeda4885e75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283728} {:answer/id #uuid "6516a4d4-b0e5-52e6-a17d-f93ce9905da5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/aa78e1ab38afbc0cd7bf92061d176a816c7a8a0e1d08c8825486c45dbe8fb5f5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283729} {:answer/id #uuid "067294cd-2914-54e2-abbc-ee5e06656f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/c95c1f93ccc6c6c2ff7264ac5bca90680ff2c3c745d95acb0f81d288bf4e498a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283730} {:answer/id #uuid "0d1c7c10-9d73-56d1-99b2-51f5c9bb8ebe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/d64f49a072fd7841d1d1b81e396673f3addcfa05005128e969dbb6ea4697d358.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afa58e3f-1404-5bee-89f4-249fd02760ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13991115/assets/39168e3de9d42254e0c1528ab7ed40f2a4c0e88e9570705b773e3875d5057df2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283727} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cf981b3-4d4d-5958-b48b-c58b6b3c7ded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6c0ad4a3-22f9-57a4-8323-31593f95cf81" :question/math-academy-id "q-81823" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059586/assets/0c2f0240b962701c2eb2ee34a0eddc164afb8e1a677a5ed7f81fe65efb890358.png)\n\nConsider the vector $v$ shown above. Find the vector $Av$ given that \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors. Computing the images of ${i,j}$ under $A$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =A(i)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =A(j)=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059586/assets/4e0e5c9cee037bded1f5739af35c3a8acfaa4d4e6f469b3e50afe69b96990e39.png)\n\nSo, the matrix represents a rotation of $\\pi $ radians (counterclockwise or clockwise) about the origin.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $Av$, we need to rotate $v$ (counterclockwise or clockwise) by an angle of $\\pi $ radians, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14059586/assets/578b3315028bf5a19a4b6e17d228db08b41f24dee63e5cb7f8d601ce667785f4.png)"}]}
